#
# E19-S01. What never enters the build context: version control, installed and built output, reports, tool state, browser
# test output, and every secret-bearing file (environment files except the example, `secrets/`, keys, `.local/`, where the
# development database port and the test-role passwords are kept). The build stage runs `COPY . .`, so anything left in
# would land in a layer of the local build cache. A pattern with no directory part matches the root of the context only,
# hence the `**/` in front of every pattern that must hold at any depth.
# scripts/docker/dockerignore.test.ts asserts each entry.
.git
node_modules
dist
coverage
reports
.vitest
.stryker-tmp
e2e
playwright-report
test-results
.local/
**/.env*
!.env.example
**/secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
*.tsbuildinfo
